Lead Scoring - Logistic Regression

Project Overview

X Education is an online education company that attracts potential customers, or leads, through various marketing channels. However, only around 30% of the leads convert into customers.

The objective of this project is to build a Logistic Regression model that can identify leads with a higher probability of conversion. The model can help the sales team prioritize leads and focus their efforts on potential customers.

Problem Statement

X Education wants to identify its most promising leads, also known as "Hot Leads".

The project aims to build a Logistic Regression model that predicts the probability of a lead converting into a customer based on factors such as lead source, website activity, occupation, previous interactions and other available information.

The original business requirement was to assign a lead score between 0 and 100, where a higher score represents a higher likelihood of conversion.

Objectives

1. Clean and prepare the lead dataset.
2. Handle missing values and irrelevant variables.
3. Convert categorical variables into numerical variables using dummy variables.
4. Split the dataset into training and testing datasets.
5. Scale relevant numerical variables.
6. Build a Logistic Regression model.
7. Use Recursive Feature Elimination (RFE) for feature selection.
8. Evaluate variables using p-values and Variance Inflation Factor (VIF).
9. Evaluate the model using accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, precision and recall.
10. Evaluate model performance using the ROC-AUC curve.
11. Identify an appropriate probability cutoff for classification.
12. Test the final model on unseen test data.

Dataset

The project uses the Leads.csv dataset provided for the X Education lead scoring case study.

The dataset contains information about leads, including:

1. Lead Origin
2. Lead Source
3. Total Visits
4. Total Time Spent on Website
5. Page Views Per Visit
6. Specialization
7. Current Occupation
8. Last Activity
9. Last Notable Activity
10. Do Not Email
11. Conversion status

The target variable is:

Converted

1. 1 = Lead converted into a customer
2. 0 = Lead did not convert

